DeviceDock

Includes serial-adapter.js, transport-native-serial.js, their synthetic regression tests,
and Rust serial.rs/lease.rs adapted from Roomen/web-serial-debug (Apache-2.0).
Original copyright and author notices are retained in LICENSE.
Changes: native ESM exports and explicit dependency injection instead of global registration;
independent DeviceDock shell configuration, no legacy authentication or update destinations.

es-module-lexer 1.7.0, Copyright Guy Bedford, MIT.
License: vendor/es-module-lexer-LICENSE. Unmodified asm.js distribution in vendor/lexer.js.

Native optional BLE and Classic SPP drivers, native-ble.js/native-classic.js,
and their regression suites are adapted from the same Apache-2.0 project.
Changes: explicit module exports, shell capability registration and DeviceDock lifecycle.
No original update URLs, login implementation or account configuration was copied.

MCP persistent configuration, updater/portable helper/signature/rollback and distribution scripts,
TEXT byte escape encoder and pure serial preset normalization are adapted from
Roomen/web-serial-debug (Apache-2.0), with DeviceDock identities and independent trust root.

xterm.js 5.5.0 and addon-fit 0.10.0 (MIT), Copyright xterm.js authors.
Licenses: vendor/xterm-LICENSE and vendor/xterm-fit-LICENSE.
ansi_up 5.1.0 (MIT), Copyright drudru; license: vendor/ansi_up-LICENSE.
Vendored distributions are unmodified; application integration is in src/log-display.js.

Windows Common Controls v6 manifest follows tauri-build 2.7.4's default
windows-app-manifest.xml (Tauri Project, Apache-2.0/MIT); all-target linker wiring
is host-owned and retains the existing Tauri icon/version resource producer.
